0a-8d8c-d627867333a4" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326304 1145 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the left side.\n\nFor the left side, we have $u=0$ and $0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ \n\nSubstituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(0\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(0,\\,0),\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/32aa42ca7dc665fb0a486f9a4f984916857d3964934c7a74c50723f1018fd833.png)" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326306 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326307 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326308 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326309 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326310 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1041 "selection" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326306 13194139535007 true] [17592186326305 1110 #uuid "c4cc789c-512d-50e8-b212-43c0683563d2" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326306 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/32aa42ca7dc665fb0a486f9a4f984916857d3964934c7a74c50723f1018fd833.png" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535007 true] [17592186326306 1111 #uuid "6e4f7035-4638-56bf-b95a-0a8f4a672bf1" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326307 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/9f3fd1164ab4346961