estion-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/a63ab6b0cb9e525901e8173ae54afb89530ae96342975731b76e51b2a51d752e.png" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535007 true] [17592186326363 1111 #uuid "075f3eb3-3f6b-5eb0-8457-44213eb29188" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326364 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/539932b6d0bc70809848bf1690df34dc56ebb569dc4877c231bd08e8698c5764.png" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535007 true] [17592186326364 1111 #uuid "31f13522-703d-5347-90a4-ac4c31e3ccf6" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326365 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/48eb6a022826e8f4e1246201e4ad190fff9bb6afdf7b2146d89010e76478a4bf.png" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535007 true] [17592186326365 1111 #uuid "f18cda0c-0738-5cfa-856e-ddcfa6a9ce4e" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326366 1034 "The image is the empty set" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535007 true] [17592186326366 1111 #uuid "436a9d83-28be-54fd-b142-8521492c4290" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326367 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326368 13194139535007 true] [17592186326367 1089 "q-161031" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326367 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535007 true] [17592186326367 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/0963fc3c56b5baac68e2d587896bf4655950640ecce5b924edc2d8e26a3e64e2.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the bottom side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\n- The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n- The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n- One endpoint of the image is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, and the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $O.$" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326367 1113 #uuid "bc24e98f-4c39-5479-a484-21b2eaa8a13f" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326367 1145 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the bottom side.\n\nFor the bottom side, we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(u,\\,0),\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/92bd315a07a5d76e77c249c12ea4544ee1555b0c214c68cf1f92fc3f07a71ddf.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡0}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $0$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\n- When $u=0,$ we obtain the point \n$(0,\\,0),$\nwhich is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane.\n\n- When $u=\\sqrt{3},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0),$\nwhose distance to $O$ is $\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo, one endpoint of the segment is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, while the other endpoint lies on the circle with radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326369 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326370 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326371 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326372 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326373 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1041 "selection" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326370 13194139535007 true] [17592186326368 1110 #uuid "f060482f-8518-56a6-850c-f026a266ac3f" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326369 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535007 true] [17592186326369 1111 #uuid "e05fcd1e-0f8f-574f-9c83-47b9a035b47b" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326370 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535007 true] [17592186326370 1111 #uuid "113ec32c-637b-5295-94e3-24b0e629d7a4" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326371 1034 "I only" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535007 true] [17592186326371 1111 #uuid "c3ebd0ca-4372-55c1-bddd-5f2ada13fa42" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326372 1034 "III only" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535007 true] [17592186326372 1111 #uuid "cea40ff5-125b-55e2-ab20-8e0c07318226" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326373 1034 "II only" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535007 true] [17592186326373 1111 #uuid "d53e305f-4453-5bc0-8e90-95ba72600102" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326374 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326375 13194139535007 true] [17592186326374 1089 "q-161035" 13194139535007 true] [17592186326374 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535007 true] [1759